\section{Parameters: units, ranges and defaults}{
\describe{
\item{\code{anchors} (wire \code{--stdin})}{string[]; required; range \samp{>= 1 anchor line; optionally a '--' line and query lines}. Two lists of tab-separated lines, group, rt_minutes, irt, split by one line holding only '--' (BULK.md section 2). No header; blank lines are skipped; a UTF-8 BOM is dropped. ANCHORS come first: one (observed retention time in minutes, library iRT) pair per line; mzLib asks for the observed apex time of confidently identified precursors (IrtCalibration.cs:29-31), and which ones is the caller's choice. A blank, NA or NaN anchor value reaches mzLib as NaN, which it refuses. QUERIES follow the '--', if any: each gives exactly one of rt_minutes (convert to iRT, IrtCalibrationModel.ToIrt) or irt (convert to minutes, ToRtMinutes) and leaves the other blank. group is any non-empty name, typically the run; each group is fitted by its own IrtCalibration.Fit call on its own anchors, and its queries are converted by that fit. Groups are reported in order of first appearance, over both lists.}
\item{\code{kind}}{string; default \code{lowess}; range \code{linear | lowess}. IrtCalibrationOptions.Kind. lowess (mzLib's default) is a robust locally weighted regression for a gradient that bends; linear is one straight line, fitted robustly. Absent sends nothing, so mzLib's default applies.}
\item{\code{minimum_anchors} (wire \code{--minimum-anchors})}{int; in \strong{anchors}; default \code{20}; range \samp{>= 3 (mzLib's own check)}. IrtCalibrationOptions.MinimumAnchors: a group with fewer anchors is refused rather than fitted. Absent means mzLib's default, 20 at the pin; the bridge sends no number of its own.}
\item{\code{bandwidth}}{float; in \strong{fraction of anchors}; default \code{0.3}; range \samp{(0, 1] (mzLib's own check)}. IrtCalibrationOptions.Bandwidth, LOWESS only: the share of a group's anchors in each local fit (at least 3). Smaller follows the gradient more closely and noise too. Absent means mzLib's default, 0.3 at the pin. mzLib checks it for linear too, and does not use it there.}
\item{\code{knots}}{int; in \strong{points}; default \code{100}; range \samp{>= 3 (mzLib's own check)}. IrtCalibrationOptions.Knots, LOWESS only: how many evenly spaced times between the first and last anchor the curve is fitted at; between them it is a straight line. Absent means mzLib's default, 100 at the pin.}
\item{\code{robustness_iterations} (wire \code{--robustness-iterations})}{int; in \strong{iterations}; default \code{3}; range \samp{>= 0 (mzLib's own check)}. IrtCalibrationOptions.RobustnessIterations: rounds of Tukey bisquare reweighting after the first fit, each downweighting anchors with large residuals. 0 keeps the first fit, which is already weighted from binned medians. Absent means mzLib's default, 3 at the pin.}
\item{\code{on_error} (wire \code{--on-error})}{string; default \code{fail}; range \code{fail | skip}. fail: the first group mzLib refuses (too few anchors, a non-finite one, anchors at one time only, or iRT that does not increase with time) stops the call with a usage error naming the group. skip: that group's error is set, its rows carry the times given and null for the rest, and the other groups are fitted. An option mzLib refuses fails the call either way.}
}
}
